# 🔐 Pre-registration files are hashed. The hashes were computed on the LF form (which is also the git blob),
# so a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true used to hand you a CRLF copy whose SHA-256 does NOT match
# PREREG_HASH*.txt. Nothing was ever wrong with the committed file; the working copy lied. Keep these LF.
introspective-accuracy/PREREG* text eol=lf
